#X obj 67 24 struct triangle01 float x float y float dx float dy float color, f 11;
#X text 160 17 A "struct" object defines the data structure named "triangle01". There can only be one "struct" object per window because the objects below \, filledpolygon etc. \, all refer back here. This struct asks for five numerical "fields" to belong to the structure \, named "x" \, "y" \, "dx" \, "dy" \, and color. The items "x" and "y" are special: they tell Pd where to place the object on the screen. The scalars in the main window both have this structure.;
#X text 334 450 ... and we draw the values of dx \, dy \, and color. To place these close to the apex of the triangle we use scale adjustments like "dx(-1000:1000)(-995:1005)" which offsets the x value by 5 pixels to (-995 \, 1005) \, and even "dy(-1000:1000)(985:-1015)" which inverts y and also offsets it by 15 units.;
#X text 62 156 The other objects in this window are drawing instructions. Each of them causes something to be drawn associated with each of the two scalars appearing in the main window. You can learn much more about them from their various "help" windows., f 89;
#X text 335 219 Here we draw a triangle whose base has coordinates (0 \, 0) and (20 \, 0) \, and an apex at the variable point (dx \, dy). Both the interior and the edge color are controlled by the "color" field. The y-coordinate is written as "dy(-1000:1000)(1000:-1000)" to map values from -1000 to 1000 into their negatives (from 1000 to -1000) - this is because "y" values in Pd normally increase downwards instead of upwards (as in most kinds of computer documents) but quantities such as magnitudes or musical pitches usually are thought to grow upward., f 59;
#X text 335 378 Here we draw the numerical values of x and y. X is drawn at coordinates (-5 \, 0) and y at coordinates (-5 \, 12). Here "12" means 12 units downward. These \, and all other coordinates \, are relative to the scalar's overall location (x \, y).;
#X text 334 605 ... and this monstrosity draws a small black rectangle at the apex of the triangle. It is meant to show where you can click to drag the apex around (changing dx and dy because the triangle's apex is variable). The leading arguments "0 0 1" specify that the outline and the interior are black and the line width is 1 .;
#X text 61 786 Useful vocabulary: a "struct" or "structure" is the abstract definition of what contents a scalar will have. The "scalar" is the object itself (there two of them in the main window). Each has five "fields": x \, y \, dx \, dy \, and color., f 81;
#X restore 463 511 pd how-it-works;
